# FastAPI Meal Planner — Cursor Rules

## Project
FastAPI + PostgreSQL backend. Anthropic generates recipes/nutrition. JWT auth. No frontend — pure JSON API.

## Stack (pinned versions)
- Python 3.11+
- fastapi==0.115.0, uvicorn[standard]==0.30.0
- SQLAlchemy==2.0.30 (async-compatible ORM), alembic==1.13.2
- psycopg[binary]==3.3.3 (psycopg3 — NOT psycopg2 syntax)
- pydantic==2.9.0, pydantic-settings==2.5.0
- passlib[bcrypt]==1.7.4, python-jose[cryptography]==3.3.0
- anthropic==0.40.0, httpx==0.27.0
- pytest==8.2.0

## Directory layout (do not deviate)
app/
  main.py          # app factory, router includes, lifespan
  config.py        # Settings via pydantic-settings (.env)
  db/
    session.py     # engine, SessionLocal, get_db dependency
    base.py        # Base + all model imports (for Alembic)
  models/          # SQLAlchemy models: chat, grocery, meal_plan, nutrition, recipe, user
  schemas/         # Pydantic v2 schemas 
  routers/         # auth, chat, grocery, meal_plans, recipes
  services/        # meal_plan_service, recipe_service, grocery_service, nutrition_service
  clients/
    anthropic_client.py   # thin SDK wrapper; methods: generate_recipes, chat_modify
  utils/
    prompt_templates.py   # all prompt strings live here, nowhere else
alembic/           # migrations only — no business logic

## Coding conventions
- Use SQLAlchemy 2.0 style (`select()`, `session.execute()`, mapped_column) — not legacy 1.x style.
- Pydantic v2 syntax only (`model_config = ConfigDict(...)`, `model_validate`, not `Config` class or `.parse_obj`).
- Settings loaded once via `pydantic-settings`; access via `from app.config import settings`. Never `os.environ` directly.
- All DB access through `get_db` dependency injection — no module-level sessions.
- Services take `db: Session` as first arg; routers call services, never ORM directly.
- JWT secret and Anthropic API key from env only — never hardcode.
- Passwords hashed with passlib bcrypt — never store plaintext.
- All endpoints require `current_user` dependency except `/auth/register` and `/auth/login`.
- Filter every query by `user_id` — no cross-user data leakage.

## Anthropic integration rules
- All SDK calls go through `AnthropicClient` in `app/clients/anthropic_client.py`.
- Model name from `settings.anthropic_model` (default `claude-3-5-sonnet-20240620`).
- Recipe generation prompts must request structured JSON output.
- Parse AI output into Pydantic schemas before any DB write; catch `ValidationError` and return 422.
- Mock `AnthropicClient` in all tests — never make real API calls in tests.
- Log request metadata (model, tokens used) but never log full prompt/response content.

## Key data relationships
User → MealPlanWeek (1:many, cascade delete)
User → Recipe (1:many, cascade delete)
User → ChatSession (1:many, cascade delete)

MealPlanWeek → PlannedMeal (1:many, cascade delete)
MealPlanWeek → GroceryList (1:many, cascade delete)

PlannedMeal → PlannedMealRecipe (1:many, cascade delete)
Recipe → PlannedMealRecipe (1:many, cascade delete)
# PlannedMeal↔Recipe is many:many via PlannedMealRecipe; PlannedMealRecipe.role = entree|side|etc.

Recipe → RecipeIngredient (1:many, cascade delete)
Recipe → NutritionInfo (1:1, uselist=False, cascade delete)
Recipe → ChatSession (1:many, cascade delete)

ChatSession → ChatMessage (1:many, cascade delete)

GroceryList → GroceryItem (1:many, cascade delete)

## Build order (follow strictly — later tasks depend on earlier)
1. setup-fastapi-project  — skeleton, config, health endpoint
2. db-and-models          — SQLAlchemy models + Alembic env
3. schemas-and-routers    — Pydantic schemas + router stubs
4. anthropic-integration  — client wrapper + prompt templates + parsing
5. grocery-and-nutrition-services — aggregation + AI nutrition
6. tests-and-docs         — pytest suite + OpenAPI cleanup

## Testing
- pytest + httpx `TestClient`; fixtures in `conftest.py`.
- Use in-memory SQLite or a test Postgres DB via env override.
- One test file per router; one per service with non-trivial logic.
- Always mock `AnthropicClient`; assert prompt content and parsed output.

## Response format
- Success: return Pydantic schema (FastAPI serializes automatically).
- 404: `raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail="...")`.
- Validation errors: let Pydantic/FastAPI return 422 automatically.
- No custom envelope wrappers (no `{"data": ..., "status": "ok"}`).

## Do not
- Do not add dependencies not in requirements.txt without explicit instruction.
- Do not put business logic in routers or prompt strings outside `prompt_templates.py`.
- Do not use `text()` raw SQL — use ORM queries.
- Do not call Anthropic API directly from routers or models.
- Do not expose password_hash in any response schema.

## Workflow reminders

- After any intentional deviation from the plan, remind me to update plan.md, README.md, and .cursorrules before ending the session.